From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:36:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: google: cpif: do not let the driver be unloaded

CPIF's platform driver has no remove(): Google builds it in or never
unloads it. module_platform_driver() still gave the module an exit
function, so rmmod would unregister the driver and free its code while
its character and network devices, notifiers and work items stayed
registered.

Register the driver from module_init() only. Without module_exit() the
module is permanent: it stays loaded until reboot.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/google/cpif/modem_main.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/modem_main.c b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/modem_main.c
index 7663c8124..041789794 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/google/cpif/modem_main.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/google/cpif/modem_main.c
@@ -987,7 +987,16 @@ static struct platform_driver cpif_driver = {
 	},
 };
 
-module_platform_driver(cpif_driver);
+/*
+ * No module_exit(): the driver has no remove(), so unbinding would leave its
+ * character and network devices, interrupts and notifiers behind. Loaded,
+ * the module stays until reboot.
+ */
+static int __init cpif_init(void)
+{
+	return platform_driver_register(&cpif_driver);
+}
+module_init(cpif_init);
 
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Exynos CP interface Driver");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
